{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T05:48:57.766Z","ordinal":82374,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a114e8-3dc1-7553-b4e3-fbed0e137776","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-817de38b-8b21-44a8-bc0f-c47dd7dee00b","process_id":"28805","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'testcenter-rewrite|optional verwendbare|protected' /Users/julian/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'testcenter-rewrite|optional verwendbare|protected' /Users/julian/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","query":"testcenter-rewrite|optional verwendbare|protected","path":"MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"260:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=verify current branch, CI, protected PPTX, and all build/integration/browser checks before a delivery claim.\n454:- Do not apply a theme based on the sister project or `iqb` realm. Unprotected `locale.currentLanguageTag` can break login when i18n is disabled; a `register.ftl` that hides global errors without field errors creates unexplained failures. Browser/production proof was not obtained. [Task 2]\n1585:- `brew install --cask rstudio` failed with `No space left on device`; account for compressed download plus unpacked app size and do not force-delete protected Prisma/npm files. [Task 1]\n2638:- Long aggregate measurements and `docker system df` can stall on a nearly full disk -> measure narrower paths and monitor/stop long processes. Do not broadly delete protected cache paths; targeted `find ... -type f -mtime +7 -delete` is safer after approval. [Task 1]\n2802:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=reuse source paths and local build/smoke guidance in this checkout; current branch, CI, protected artifact, and parity status need fresh verification.\n2827:- for an “optional verwendbare, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche” -> retain Rewrite UI and shared backend/session semantics; use explicit reversible interface selection rather than replacing the default. [Task 2]\n3292:- ContentPool is the hub for standardized Assessment Content Packages: take in, validate, version, review, control release, and transfer ACPs. It is not a general authoring environment and does not automatically repair content; primary authoring belongs in IQB-Studio. The official scenarios are public provision, protected delivery, intermediate storage/backup with server transfer, review with comments, and Item-Sichtung/Standard Setting. [Task 1]\n3329:- Broad `rm -rf` against caches produced mass `Permission denied` errors in `node-gyp` -> skip protected paths, suppress expected permission noise, and clean selected cache directories with targeted `find ... -delete`; do not force the remaining roughly 263 MB without administrator authorization. [Task 1]\n4145:- Credential access is capped at three months, which conflicts with a possible 18-month retention requirement. Delivered estimate: 8–12 person-days current-stand read-only; 18–28 protected archive with immutable state/retention; +6–12 PDF/print; overall about 20–30 person-days without robust PDF or 30–40 with it, plus 1–3 concept/workshop days. [Task 1]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"260:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=verify current branch, CI, protected PPTX, and all build/integration/browser checks before a delivery claim.\n454:- Do not apply a theme based on the sister project or `iqb` realm. Unprotected `locale.currentLanguageTag` can break login when i18n is disabled; a `register.ftl` that hides global errors without field errors creates unexplained failures. Browser/production proof was not obtained. [Task 2]\n1585:- `brew install --cask rstudio` failed with `No space left on device`; account for compressed download plus unpacked app size and do not force-delete protected Prisma/npm files. [Task 1]\n2638:- Long aggregate measurements and `docker system df` can stall on a nearly full disk -> measure narrower paths and monitor/stop long processes. Do not broadly delete protected cache paths; targeted `find ... -type f -mtime +7 -delete` is safer after approval. [Task 1]\n2802:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=reuse source paths and local build/smoke guidance in this checkout; current branch, CI, protected artifact, and parity status need fresh verification.\n2827:- for an “optional verwendbare, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche” -> retain Rewrite UI and shared backend/session semantics; use explicit reversible interface selection rather than replacing the default. [Task 2]\n3292:- ContentPool is the hub for standardized Assessment Content Packages: take in, validate, version, review, control release, and transfer ACPs. It is not a general authoring environment and does not automatically repair content; primary authoring belongs in IQB-Studio. The official scenarios are public provision, protected delivery, intermediate storage/backup with server transfer, review with comments, and Item-Sichtung/Standard Setting. [Task 1]\n3329:- Broad `rm -rf` against caches produced mass `Permission denied` errors in `node-gyp` -> skip protected paths, suppress expected permission noise, and clean selected cache directories with targeted `find ... -delete`; do not force the remaining roughly 263 MB without administrator authorization. [Task 1]\n4145:- Credential access is capped at three months, which conflicts with a possible 18-month retention requirement. Delivered estimate: 8–12 person-days current-stand read-only; 18–28 protected archive with immutable state/retention; +6–12 PDF/print; overall about 20–30 person-days without robust PDF or 30–40 with it, plus 1–3 concept/workshop days. [Task 1]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9834},"formatted_output":"260:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=verify current branch, CI, protected PPTX, and all build/integration/browser checks before a delivery claim.\n454:- Do not apply a theme based on the sister project or `iqb` realm. Unprotected `locale.currentLanguageTag` can break login when i18n is disabled; a `register.ftl` that hides global errors without field errors creates unexplained failures. Browser/production proof was not obtained. [Task 2]\n1585:- `brew install --cask rstudio` failed with `No space left on device`; account for compressed download plus unpacked app size and do not force-delete protected Prisma/npm files. [Task 1]\n2638:- Long aggregate measurements and `docker system df` can stall on a nearly full disk -> measure narrower paths and monitor/stop long processes. Do not broadly delete protected cache paths; targeted `find ... -type f -mtime +7 -delete` is safer after approval. [Task 1]\n2802:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=reuse source paths and local build/smoke guidance in this checkout; current branch, CI, protected artifact, and parity status need fresh verification.\n2827:- for an “optional verwendbare, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche” -> retain Rewrite UI and shared backend/session semantics; use explicit reversible interface selection rather than replacing the default. [Task 2]\n3292:- ContentPool is the hub for standardized Assessment Content Packages: take in, validate, version, review, control release, and transfer ACPs. It is not a general authoring environment and does not automatically repair content; primary authoring belongs in IQB-Studio. The official scenarios are public provision, protected delivery, intermediate storage/backup with server transfer, review with comments, and Item-Sichtung/Standard Setting. [Task 1]\n3329:- Broad `rm -rf` against caches produced mass `Permission denied` errors in `node-gyp` -> skip