{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T06:20:50.407Z","ordinal":82899,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a11505-6069-7411-b5ab-e7c10a97a630","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dab7e151-e30d-4d1b-9954-e8666889d86d","process_id":"66969","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n## testcenter-rewrite-parity...origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\n M rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M rewrite-app/package.json\n M rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? rewrite-app/docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? rewrite-app/scripts/participant-entry-selection.test.mjs\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n## testcenter-rewrite-parity...origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\n M rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M rewrite-app/package.json\n M rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? rewrite-app/docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? rewrite-app/scripts/participant-entry-selection.test.mjs\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7375},"formatted_output":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n## testcenter-rewrite-parity...origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\n M rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\n M rewrite-app/package.json\n M rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\n?? rewrite-app/docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n?? rewrite-app/scripts/participant-entry-selection.test.mjs\n"},"started_at_ms":1791354050407,"completed_at_ms":1791354050407}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T06:20:50.414Z","ordinal":82900,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11505-976e-7a32-8b7e-bf2eb7edf124","call_id":"call_cc35a40239954ff5b911c6a83d0b10df","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"chunk_id\":\"5200d5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1831,\"output\":\"---\\nname: playwright\\ndescription: \\\"Browser automation with Playwright. Use when the user asks to test a website, take screenshots, check responsive design, test login flows, fill forms, check broken links, or automate any browser task.\\\"\\nmetadata:\\n  version: 1.0.0\\n---\\n\\n# Playwright (Browser Automation)\\n\\nGeneral-purpose browser automation skill. Write custom Playwright scripts for any automation task and execute them via the universal executor.\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\nAny user request involving browser testing, web automation, screenshots, responsive design checks, form testing, link validation, login flow testing, or any other browser-based task.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### 1. Resolve skill directory\\n\\nThis skill can be installed in different locations (plugin system, manual installation, global, or project-specific). Determine the skill directory based on where this SKILL.md was loaded. Use that path as `$SKILL_DIR` in all commands below.\\n\\n### 2. Setup (first time only)\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && npm run setup\\n```\\n\\nInstalls Playwright and Chromium. Only needed once.\\n\\n### 3. Detect dev servers\\n\\nFor localhost testing, always detect running servers first:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && node -e \\\"require('./lib/helpers').detectDevServers().then(servers => console.log(JSON.stringify(servers)))\\\"\\n```\\n\\n| Result | Action |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| 1 server found | Use it automatically, inform user |\\n| Multiple servers found | Ask user which one to test |\\n| No servers found | Ask for URL or offer to help start dev server |\\n\\n### 4. Write the test script\\n\\nWrite custom Playwright code to `/tmp/playwright-test-*.js`. Never write test files to the skill directory or user's project.\\n\\nRules:\\n- Parameterize URLs — put detected/provided URL in a `TARGET_URL` constant at top\\n- Use `headless: false` by default — only use headless when user explicitly requests it\\n- Use `slowMo: 100` for visibility when helpful\\n\\n### 5. Execute\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && node run.js /tmp/playwright-test-page.js\\n```\\n\\nFor quick one-off tasks, execute inline without creating files:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && node run.js \\\"\\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false });\\nconst page = await browser.newPage();\\nawait page.goto('http://localhost:3001');\\nawait page.screenshot({ path: '/tmp/quick-screenshot.png', fullPage: true });\\nconsole.log('Screenshot saved');\\nawait browser.close();\\n\\\"\\n```\\n\\n| Input method | When to use |\\n|-------------|-------------|\\n| File (`/tmp/playwright-test-*.js`) | Complex tests, responsive checks, anything user might re-run |\\n| Inline string | Quick one-off tasks (screenshot, check element, get page title) |\\n\\n### 6. Report results\\n\\nDisplay results in real-time. Browser window is visible for debugging. Test files in `/tmp` are auto-cleaned by the OS.\\n\\n## Common Patterns\\n\\n### Test a page (multiple viewports)\\n\\n```javascript\\n// /tmp/playwright-test-responsive.js\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3001'; // Auto-detected\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, slowMo: 100 });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  // Desktop test\\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1920, height: 1080 });\\n  await page.goto(TARGET_URL);\\n  console.log('Desktop - Title:', await page.title());\\n  await page.screenshot({ path: '/tmp/desktop.png', fullPage: true });\\n\\n  // Mobile test\\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 375, height: 667 });\\n  await page.screenshot({ path: '/tmp/mobile.png', fullPage: true });\\n\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n### Test login flow\\n\\n```javascript\\n// /tmp/playwright-test-login.js\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3001'; // Auto-detected\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  await page.goto(`${TARGET_URL}/login`);\\n\\n  await page.fill('input[name=\\\"email\\\"]', 'test@example.com');\\n  await page.fill('input[name=\\\"password\\\"]', 'password123');\\n  await page.click('button[type=\\\"submit\\\"]');\\n\\n  // Wait for redirect\\n  await page.waitForURL('**/dashboard');\\n  console.log('Login successful, redirected to dashboard');\\n\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n### Fill and submit form\\n\\n```javascript\\n// /tmp/playwright-test-form.js\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3001'; // Auto-detected\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, slowMo: 50 });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  await page.goto(`${TARGET_URL}/contact`);\\n\\n  await page.fill('input[name=\\\"name\\\"]', 'John Doe');\\n  await page.fill('input[name=\\\"email\\\"]', 'john@example.com');\\n  await page.fill('textarea[name=\\\"message\\\"]', 'Test message');\\n  await page.click('button[type=\\\"submit\\\"]');\\n\\n  // Verify submission\\n  await page.waitForSelector('.success-message');\\n  console.log('Form submitted successfully');\\n\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n### Check for broken links\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  await page.goto('http://localhost:3000');\\n\\n  const links = await page.locator('a[href^=\\\"http\\\"]').all();\\n  const results = { working: 0, broken: [] };\\n\\n  for (const link of links) {\\n    const href = await link.getAttribute('href');\\n    try {\\n      const response = await page.request.head(href);\\n      if (response.ok()) {\\n        results.working++;\\n      } else {\\n        results.broken.push({ url: href, status: response.status() });\\n      }\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      results.broken.push({ url: href, error: e.message });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  console.log(`Working links: ${results.working}`);\\n  console.log(`Broken links:`, results.broken);\\n\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n### Take screenshot with error handling\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  try {\\n    await page.goto('http://localhost:3000', {\\n      waitUntil: 'networkidle',\\n      timeout: 10000,\\n    });\\n\\n    await page.screenshot({\\n      path: '/tmp/screenshot.png',\\n      fullPage: true,\\n    });\\n\\n    console.log('Screenshot saved to /tmp/screenshot.png');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error('Error:', error.message);\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n### Test responsive design\\n\\n```javascript\\n// /tmp/playwright-test-responsive-full.js\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst TARGET_URL = 'http://localhost:3001'; // Auto-detected\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n\\n  const viewports = [\\n    { name: 'Desktop', width: 1920, height: 1080 },\\n    { name: 'Tablet', width: 768, height: 1024 },\\n    { name: 'Mobile', width: 375, height: 667 },\\n  ];\\n\\n  for (const viewport of viewports) {\\n    console.log(\\n      `Testing ${viewport.name} (${viewport.width}x${viewport.height})`,\\n    );\\n\\n    await page.setViewportSize({\\n      width: viewport.width,\\n      height: viewport.height,\\n    });\\n\\n    await page.goto(TARGET_URL);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1000);\\n\\n    await page.screenshot({\\n      path: `/tmp/${viewport.name.toLowerCase()}.png`,\\n      fullPage: true,\\n    });\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"chunk_id\":\"ed4765\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":80,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\nrewrite-spike/README.md\\nREADME.md\\nrewrite-app/scripts/participant-entry-selection.test.mjs\\nrewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\nrewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\\nrewrite-app/README.md\\nrewrite-app/test-fixtures/original-testcenter/README.md\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"chunk_id\":\"fbc4c8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":98,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n## testcenter-rewrite-parity...origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\\n M rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts\\n M rewrite-app/package.json\\n M rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\\n?? rewrite-app/docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\\n?? rewrite-app/scripts/participant-entry-selection.test.mjs\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"chunk_id\":\"0b8a07\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1751,\"output\":\"const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\\nconst { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\\nconst { mkdtemp } = require('node:fs/promises');\\nconst { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\\nconst { join } = require('node:path');\\nconst { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\nconst APP_ROOT = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\\nconst TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\\nassert.ok(TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, 'Select an immutable frontend before testing.');\\nconst owned = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-entry-target-'));\\nconst server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\\n  import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(pathToFileURL(`${APP_ROOT}/apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js`).href)};\\n  const server = await createProductionApiServer();\\n  server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\\n  process.once('SIGTERM', () => server.close(() => process.exit(0)));\\n`], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, env: { ...process.env,\\n  FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(owned, 'store.sqlite'),\\n  FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\\n  FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'legacy-compatibility', FIRST_SLICE_PROOF_OF_WORK_SCOPES: ''\\n}, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'] });\\nlet browser;\\ntry {\\n  const port = await new Promise((done, reject) => {\\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out.')), 20000);\\n    server.once('message', message => { clearTimeout(timer); done(message.port); });\\n    server.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\\n    server.once('exit', () => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited.')); });\\n  });\\n  const TARGET_URL = `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`;\\n  let operator;\\n  const api = async (path, body, token = operator) => {\\n    const result = await fetch(`${TARGET_URL}${path}`, {\\n      method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', ...(token ? { authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } : {}) },\\n      ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) })\\n    });\\n    assert.ok(result.ok, `${path}: HTTP ${result.status}`);\\n    return result.json();\\n  };\\n  operator = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\\n  await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'entry-target', displayName: 'Owned entry target' });\\n  const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/entry-target';\\n  const source = await api(`${workspace}/source-packages`, { fileName: 'entry.json', mediaType: 'application/json', contentStructure: {\\n    bookletEntries: [{ bookletKey: 'entry-booklet', displayLabel: 'Entry booklet', unitEntries: [{ unitKey: 'entry-unit', displayLabel: 'Entry unit', content: 'Owned answer fixture' }] }]\\n  }});\\n  const imported = await api(`${workspace}/import-jobs`, { sourcePackageId: source.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\\n  await api(`${workspace}/content-releases/${imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId}/activate`, {});\\n  await api(`${workspace}/participant-roster`, { rosterText: ['old-login', 'new-login'].map(loginKey => ({\\n    loginKey, groupKey: 'entry-group', bookletKey: 'entry-booklet', displayName: loginKey, executionMode: 'run-hot-return'\\n  })) });\\n  browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: process.env.CI === 'true', channel: process.env.TEST_BROWSER_CHANNEL || undefined });\\n  for (const ui of ['rewrite', 'original']) {\\n    const context = await browser.newContext();\\n    const page = await context.newPage();\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\\n    await page.goto(`${TARGET_URL}/app/participant?ui=rewrite&tenantKey=demo-tenant&workspaceKey=entry-target`, { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n    await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill('old-login');\\n    const identityResponse = page.waitForResponse(response => new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in' && response.request().method() === 'POST');\\n    await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\\n    const identity = await (await identityResponse).json();\\n    if (!(await page.locator('#participantRouteStatus').textContent())?.includes('running')) {\\n      await page.locator('#participantRouteStartOrResumeButton').click();\\n    }\\n    await page.locator('#participantRouteStatus', { hasText: 'running' }).waitFor();\\n    const old = (await api(`/api/v1/participant/sessions/${identity.participantSession.participantSessionId}/current-state`, undefined, identity.sessionToken)).currentRunState.testRun;\\n    const answer = '  preserved previous answer ä漢字\\\\n';\\n    await api(`/api/v1/participant/test-runs/${old.testRunId}/save-progress`, { status: 'running', responseUnitKey: 'entry-unit', unitResponse: answer }, identity.sessionToken);\\n    // Reproduce the operator's preselection of login fields while retaining its\\n    // cached old session. Actual participant credentials came from browser login.\\n    await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const key = 'testcenter-rewrite-app-shell';\\n      const snapshot = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key));\\n      assertNotNeeded = undefined;\\n      localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify({ ...snapshot, loginKey: 'new-login', groupKey: 'entry-group', bookletKey: 'entry-booklet' }));\\n    });\\n    const popup = await context.newPage();\\n    popup.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\\n    await popup.goto(`${TARGET_URL}/participant?${new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'entry-target', loginKey: 'new-login', groupKey: 'entry-group', bookletKey: 'entry-booklet' })}`, { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n    await popup.locator('#participantRouteStatus', { hasText: 'running' }).waitFor();\\n    const actual = await popup.evaluate(() => ({ login: document.querySelector('#participantLoginKey')?.value,\\n      session: document.querySelector('#participantRouteSessionId')?.value,\\n      run: document.querySelector('#participantRouteRunId')?.textContent?.trim() }));\\n    console.log(`entry_target=${ui}:${JSON.stringify(actual)}`);\\n    assert.equal(actual.login, 'new-login');\\n    assert.notEqual(actual.session, identity.participantSession.participantSessionId);\\n    assert.notEqual(actual.run, old.testRunId);\\n    const retained = (await api(`/api/v1/participant/sessions/${identity.participantSession.participantSessionId}/current-state?testRunId=${old.testRunId}`, undefined, identity.sessionToken)).currentRunState.testRun;\\n    assert.equal(retained.status, 'running');\\n    assert.equal(retained.unitResponses['entry-unit'], answer);\\n    assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\\n    await context.close();\\n  }\\n} finally {\\n  await browser?.close();\\n  if (server.exitCode === null) {\\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\\n    await new Promise(done => server.once('exit', done));\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":4,\"chunk_id\":\"65c7fb\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000016292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":5,\"goal\":{\"threadId\":\"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a\",\"objective\":\"Testcenter Rewrite bis zur nachgewiesenen vollständigen Parität fertigstellen, einschließlich einer optional verwendbaren, mit der Original-UI identischen Oberfläche; offene Fehler testen, sinnvolle Schritte committen und mit aktuellen Entire-Checkpoints auf GitHub pushen, private Testdaten und geschützte PPTX bewahren.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"tokensUsed\":10191493,\"timeUsedSeconds\":74412,\"createdAt\":1789189722,\"updatedAt\":1791354050},\"remainingTokens\":null,\"completionBudgetReport\":null}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11505-6069-7411-b5ab-e7c10a97a630","create_time":1791354050.413999}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
