age_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791357180.372559,"turn_id":"01a11526-9c9a-7463-b440-efbb190b92c4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.5 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ee6663\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":21,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"artifact_type\\\":\\\"pull_request\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite/pull/1\\\"}\"}],\"isError\":false}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"749385\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.189891292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":60,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n● Enabled · branch testcenter-rewrite-parity\\n  Agents · Codex\\n  Checkpoints sync to: origin\\nAgents: run `entire agent-help` for machine-readable usage.\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1b3923\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.489923541,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":85,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"counts\\\":[{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"count\\\":6,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"count\\\":17,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"count\\\":12,\\\"status\\\":\\\"queued\\\"}],\\\"headSha\\\":\\\"03e660aea271813ac4aae99e5d48a3fa47c15791\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"queued\\\"}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac5f0fefaf481919726e45a7b90b5d2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11526-9c9a-7463-b440-efbb190b92c4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Die Testlauf-Links in Study Monitor und Content sind korrigiert und mit Commit `03e660ae` gepusht.\n\n- 285 Unit-/Frontend-Tests, Typecheck und Produktionsbuild grün.\n- Browserprüfung in beiden Oberflächen sowie vollständiger SQLite-Browserlauf grün.\n- Beide neuen Entire-Checkpoints auf GitHub verifiziert.\n- Private Testdaten und PPTX unverändert.\n\nDie [Remote-CI](https://github.com/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite/actions/runs/37585853547) läuft noch. Kein Merge, noch keine 100 %. Nächster Schritt: mehrere unvollständige Testhefte sicher starten und getrennt fortsetzen.\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:2826-2837|note=[Shared interface semantics and separate full CI and UI acceptance]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","type":"output_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":336},"id":"msg_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac5f104087881918881b7e54d850a7c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1791357180.970046,"turn_id":"01a11526-9c9a-7463-b440-efbb190b92c4"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ich arbeite jetzt am Wechsel zwischen mehreren unvollständigen Testheften. Dafür müssen Start und Wiederaufnahme die genaue Zuweisung auswählen und konkurrierende Starts denselben Lauf wiederverwenden. Antworten, Timer und Monitor-Sperren dürfen dabei nicht zwischen den Läufen vermischt werden.\n","type":"output_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":337},"id":"msg_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac5f10e8ea4819196701ce6cde79779","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1791357194.374867,"turn_id":"01a11535-8d28-7f81-ae24-42a0de06e27f"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_M11MW8NigJzxxeNPQOQlRxbb","id":"ctc_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac5f111b1fc8191904a9057c1ef7203","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git status --short --branch\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite\",max_output_tokens:1600}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n 'Newly reproduced multi-Booklet|atomic|available.*in_progress' docs/PARITY.md\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",max_output_tokens:1600}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n 'testcenter-rewrite|selected-run' /Users/julian/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -12\",max_output_tokens:2300}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh run view 37585853547 --repo jurei733/testcenter-rewrite --json status,conclusion,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,counts:([.jobs[]|{status,conclusion}]|group_by(.status,.conclusion)|map({status:.[0].status,conclusion:.[0].conclusion,count:length}))}'\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite\",max_output_tokens:1800}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '32855,32915p' packages/application/src/index.ts\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",max_output_tokens:2600}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '33775,33800p' packages/application/src/index.ts\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",max_output_tokens:1500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1290,1325p' packages/file-store/src/index.ts\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",max_output_tokens:2200}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '660,720p' packages/memory-store/src/index.ts\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",max_output_tokens:2500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791357194.374867,"turn_id":"01a11535-8d28-7f81-ae24-42a0de06e27f"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_M11MW8NigJzxxeNPQOQlRxbb","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a11535-d11b-79c1-8e17-f28769bafccd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791357210.907458,"turn_id":"01a11535-8d28-7f81-ae24-42a0de06e27f"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"47e4cc\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":52,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n## testcenter-rewrite-parity...origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\\n?? rewrite-app/docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"3299ff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":9230,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9230)\\nTotal output lines: 22\\n\\n/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n208:### Newly reproduced multi-Booklet starter gap (P0, open)\\n219:use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself and atomic per-assignment\\n275:Presence and the corresponding log commit atomically in every repository.\\n832:  installation matching and PostgreSQL startup/import atomicity. PHP-specific\\n1271:| Configurable password and proof-of-work policy | 18.2 `Password`, `SessionController`, `/session/challenge`, `/session/person/challenge` | done | P1 | the rewrite applies one deployment-configurable administrator-password minimum and JavaScript regular-expression rule to every password write while preserving sign-in for existing passwords after policy changes. Optional SHA-256 browser proof of work is independently selectable for administrator credentials, all participant logins, and second codes; the global admin and participant scopes also prevent an omitted required password from cheaply filling their failure sinks. Angular uses `altcha-lib` Workers like the Original. Signed short-lived tokens bind a keyed credential digest without exposing the credential, accept only the current or explicitly configured previous key ID, and are atomically consumed in memory/file/SQLite/Postgres. Startup and preflight validate scopes, secret length, distinct rotation keys, work range, and TTL; secret-free runtime configuration drives disabled-mode-compatible clients. Unit/API gates cover credential binding, expiry, replay, controlled rotation, redaction, password-omission resistance, and rate-limit composition, while production SQLite/Chromium proves all three scopes end to end |\\n1291:| 2 | P0 | Adaptive and runtime-policy corpus | Exercise broader production coding schemes and nested combinations of adaptive states, timers, completeness locks, code gates, and leave-once navigation across the durable-store and browser gates. The byte-exact current frontend controller fixture closes the nested Root/outer/inner timer, two-stage code, and dimension-specific completeness precedence. A schema-conformant extension of the hash-pinned current `CY_Bklt_Adap-1` production package proves that hidden-route restrictions stay dormant and that its real coding-driven professional route activates code, timer, response completeness, allowed timer leave, and testlet leave-once atomically across memory, file, and SQLite. A dedicated production-built SQLite/Chromium gate now drives the same current Player through the visible Beginner-to-Professional reroute, code entry, timer/leave-lock presentation, completeness denial, successful allowed leave, and disabled locked re-entry. Broader production schemes and packages remain. |\\n1293:| 4 | P1 | Workspace batch edge cases | Add broader replacement graphs outside the now-guarded import/assembly paths. Guided ambiguity diagnostics carry an opaque revision of the exact workspace file population shown to the operator; every selected retry must echo it, and any intervening replacement/upload/delete fails closed as `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale` until the ambiguity is refreshed. The final automatic dependency snapshot and m…7630 tokens truncated…-target reauthorization and audit trail, with successful targets removed and concrete failures retained for retry; API coverage verifies deduplication plus mixed success/self/missing results, and a SQLite browser gate revokes two live delegated sessions. Permanent user deletion now reuses the same 50-account exact selection and per-target delegation boundary, prevents self-delete, requires irreversible-action confirmation, removes every successful account with all sessions and role assignments in one store transaction, retains concrete failures for retry, and records a standalone audit snapshot with the deleted username, display/status/roles, and exact removal counts. API coverage proves authentication, self-protection, session invalidation, repeat-delete behavior, directory cleanup, and audit retention across the durable stores; a real SQLite browser gate deletes two delegated accounts and verifies their directory/session absence plus both retained audits. All Ops account, role, password, session, access-window, custom-text, and monitor-profile confirmations now share a labelled in-app alert dialog with safe initial focus, trapped keyboard navigation, Escape cancellation, focus restoration, and explicit action-specific confirmation. The protected production browser gates exercise the no-request cancel path and the representative single and batch confirmation sequence through account deletion. Original workspace lifecycle parity now covers creation, RW/RO assignment, rename, and platform-admin-only permanent deletion. Deletion requires the exact workspace key, atomically clears every workspace aggregate and scoped role, retains the global audit record, and is gated across memory/file/SQLite plus protected Chromium/SQLite. Matching the original three-tab system administration, platform admins now switch through one responsive, keyboard-visible `Admins` / `Workspaces` / `Settings` navigation shared by Ops and Workspace routes. Admin and Settings panels are mutually exclusive, the selected panel is URL-stable, and production Chromium gates the complete settings-to-workspace-to-admin round-trip. The workspace directory now also reproduces the Original table's `MAX(files.modification_ts)` signal from currently stored source-package upload times, keeps empty workspaces explicit, exports the value, and sorts interactively by name or latest file modification in either direction. The 18 upstream Superadmin E2E scenarios are now explicitly traced: all settings controls plus maintenance-warning set/clear; user action availability, creation, invalid/valid Superadmin step-up, RO/RW enforcement, password mismatch/success, and deletion; and workspace action availability, creation, user-centred RO/RW assignment, rename, and deletion. Rewrite API and production SQLite/Chromium gates cover every path, so the Original Superadmin surface is functionally closed; the additional tenant hierarchy, access windows, batch operations, session administration, CSVs, and audit evidence exceed that baseline. |\\n2779:limits, and replace or clear it atomically from a transient JSON editor. The\\n2804:monitor, audit, or session mutation. Its small atomic core file now commits an\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0aa875\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":340,\"output\":\"260:applies_to: cwd=/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app; reuse_rule=verify current branch, CI, protected PPTX, and all build/integration/browser checks before a delivery claim.\\n266:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-07T17-47-44-rcM2-participant_run_selection_and_live_update_isolation.md (cwd=/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code, rollout_path=/Users/julian/.codex/sessions/2026/09/07/rollout-2026-09-07T19-47-44-01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T07:51:13+00:00, thread_id=01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a, partial; Revi