nd SQLite. The current two-Booklet/four-Unit Aspect graph and changed 18.0 roster likewise gate the new Unit, full dependency retention, symbol-keypad settings, second-code enforcement, and the real multi-booklet `testuser1` flow across all three stores. The complete official `@iqb/responses` 3.6.0 `test/coding/derive` tree is additionally pinned through 11 scheme variants and all 23 byte-exact inputs/outcomes. A combined compatibility package gates `CONCAT_CODE`, `COPY_VALUE`, `MANUAL`, all four `SOLVER` variants, `SUM_CODE`, `SUM_SCORE`, and `UNIQUE_VALUES`, including aliases, same-ID/no-alias solvers, dependency failures, arrays, copied unset values, partial inputs, explicit zeroes, and every official status/value/code/score route through import, server coding, adaptive routing, and raw-response retention across memory, file, and SQLite. The historical DAN `G231mm.xml` + `G231mm.voud` + metadata-free `IQBVisualUnitPlayerV2.99.2.html` graph now has prebuilt and loose intake gates plus a production SQLite/Chromium execution gate for its API-2.1 handshake, JSON-string `all` response, and reload restoration; dotted version suffixes resolve only as a conservative metadata-free filename fallback, and competing versions remain an explicit ambiguity. Its complete original three-unit Aspect booklet, IQB Aspect 2.12.3 player, and all Unit/Voud pairs add a production-sized import and browser handshake/save/navigation/restore gate, including a 16.17 MB media definition; operational monitor/system-check logins are excluded from participant import\nREADME.md:955:- the official `array-length-check` and deliberately versionless `arrays` schemes from `@iqb/responses` 3.6.0 pin all six historical cases and gate AND-connected rulesets, `ANY_OPEN`, `LENGTH`, `SORT_ARRAY`, numeric array positions, `SUM`, `ANY_OTHER`, `ANY`, sorted array comparison, automatic zero coding, derived `SUM_SCORE`, and `CODING_INCOMPLETE` routing across memory, file, and SQLite\nREADME.md:958:- together with the root `alias` and `subforms` cases, the compatibility corpus now pins the complete official `@iqb/responses` 3.6.0 `test/coding` tree: 34 scheme variants and all 70 byte-exact inputs/outcomes. Base aliases route by their external identifiers; ordered repeated-ID subform responses reach the IQB coder with their `subform` markers intact, while `BASE_NO_VALUE` remains omitted and the adaptive Testcenter read model deliberately applies its original ID-only last-write selection after coding. The unchanged multi-subform Player envelope, final coded status/value/code/score route, and persistence are gated across memory, file, and SQLite\nREADME.md:960:- the pinned original `SysCheck.xml` and byte-exact official `CY_SysCheck_2.xml` import as first-class system-check definitions without producing empty content releases. Multiple checks remain independently selectable in one workspace; the browser gate proves the measured-network and configured-`skipnetwork` paths, required-field feedback, every original questionnaire control, two resolved Verona runs, save-key reports, statistics, and check-isolated cleanup. Separately uploaded SysCheck, Unit, IQB coding-scheme, and Verona files resolve transitively into audited immutable packages; their Unit definition and Player stay attached to each check, and a packaged missing Unit is rejected with a stable diagnostic. `/system-check` is a lazy direct-entry Angular flow for browser/device capture, configured repeated upload/download throughput against original-compatible `/speed-test/random-package` endpoints, application latency and connection hints, original threshold ratings, per-check `syscheck_*` custom texts, Original report cancellation, and report persistence. Matching the Original welcome check, a cache-disabled public server-time contract compares the browser clock and IANA timezone with the configured participant timezone; deviations of at least 60 seconds and timezone mismatches are highlighted and retained in the saved environment report, while an unavailable check remains visible as a warning. The Original 800 × 600 minimum screen resolution is evaluated and highlighted in the same report. The Original's UAParser-based CPU architecture, device model/type/vendor, browser and major version, operating system and version, cookie/language/core values, and available browser-plugin names are captured with the upstream report labels and stable IDs, sorted by label, persisted, and included in both report detail and semicolon CSV export. Scoped operators can list/filter reports, export original-style semicolon CSV columns, inspect per-check operating-system/browser/overall-rating distributions and individual report values, and delete selected report sets only after typing the workspace key; deletion is store-scoped and audited across memory, file, and SQLite. Creating the first dedicated system-check account removes anonymous key-based entry instance-wide; after its mandatory password rotation, the protected browser flow auto-selects a single assigned check, validates required questions, hides the report-title and save-key inputs, and proves that the saved report title is forced to the login name\nREADME.md:961:- destructive Angular actions no longer depend on browser-native `confirm` or `prompt` UI. Workspace/content/result/system-check exact-value gates and ordinary monitor/admin confirmations share a labelled in-app alert dialog with safe initial focus, focus trapping/restoration, Escape cancellation, preserved multiline/custom monitor copy, and a disabled destructive action until the exact workspace/group/file value is entered. Participant review deletion reuses the Player confirmation surface. Production SQLite/Chromium gates prove wrong-text rejection, cancellation without a request, focus restoration, exact acceptance, and the representative content, monitor, system-check, review, and admin paths\nREADME.md:965:- byte-preserving XML intake recognizes UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32, ISO-8859, Windows, CJK, and other legacy declarations across direct uploads, Data URLs, loose dependency assembly, and ZIP entries. XML-standard `ISO-10646-UCS-2` and `ISO-10646-UCS-4` aliases map onto the signature-aware UTF-16/32 decoders instead of being rejected as unknown; generic aliases accept either byte order only when the BOM or leading XML signature agrees. A production `iconv-lite` fallback extends Node's narrower WHATWG decoder set with allowlisted `ISO-8859-16`/Latin-10 and DOS `CP437`/`CP775`/`CP850`/`CP852`/`CP858` IANA aliases without admitting transport codecs such as base64, hex, or UTF-7 as XML encodings. Supported multibyte encodings are decoded strictly: incomplete UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32, Shift_JIS, and other WHATWG sequences fail with `source_document_xml_encoding_invalid_bytes` instead of entering normalization as replacement characters. Data-URL charset metadata remains authoritative when an XML declaration is absent. Original-corpus API gates preserve representative Romanian, German, Baltic, Czech, Cyrillic, Japanese, simplified/traditional Chinese, Korean, and Euro labels through the complete release projection across memory, file, and SQLite alongside a big-endian UCS-2 Booklet, a little-endian UCS-4 Booklet, a UCS-4 IMS manifest inside ZIP, and malformed multibyte rejection\nREADME.md:967:- ZIP imports now perform version-aware structural validation of bundled Verona `application/ld+json` metadata for the early `@id`/`@type`/`apiVersion` draft, the experimental `$schema`-only shape without `metadataVersion`, legacy 1.x/2.x, and strict 3.0/3.1 documents before staging: malformed/non-player documents, unsupported metadata or API versions, invalid core/nested fields, and player-reference/module-version/id mismatches fail with stable diagnostics. Unit references use `player-id@module-version`; `apiVersion` in the early draft and `specVersion` in later generations independently declare Verona API compatibility. A narrow, warning-bearing metadata-3.1 compatibility path accepts the official Lottie 1.2.2 release's legacy `$schema`, lowercase module type, `notSupportedFeatures`, and singleton dependency object only after structural validation; unrelated unknown fields remain invalid. Metadata-free legacy players remain importable with a stable warning because their reference cannot prove API compatibility, and the runtime ready handshake remains authoritative. The official `verona-player-simple` releases 1.0.1, 2.1.0, 4.0.0, and 5.2.0 negotiating APIs 2.1.0, 3.0.0, 4.0, and 5.2, the historical official ABI `3.3.0` scripted-survey Player negotiating API `2.1.0`, the current ABI `5.0.0` release declaring spec `5.0` while negotiating runtime API `4`, historical DAN `3.0.0` negotiating API `2.1.0`, and current DAN `3.1.0` declaring spec `5.0` while negotiating runtime API `4`, the historical official Speedtest `1.2.0` Player declaring spec `5.0` while negotiating runtime API `4`, the current official Speedtest `3.3.0` Player negotiating API `5.2`, the official Lottie `1.2.2` Player negotiating API `6.0`, the independent STARS `0.6.19` and current official STARS `0.7.2` packages plus the complete current Original STARS `0.6.40` system-test package negotiating API `6.0`, the original Verona 6 fixture, the full original Aspect `2.12.3` module and current official Aspect `2.12.6` release negotiating API `6.0`, all supported metadata generations, and a metadata-free browser player are executable compatibility gates. Current ABI additionally gates its `iqb-scripted@1.0` definition and JSON-string `allData` carrying `iqb-standard@1.1`; current DAN gates its release-tag/embedded-`3.1.0-beta` version boundary plus historical `IQBVisualUnitPlayerV2.1.0` JSON-string `all` state; current Speedtest gates its published definition-type/version mismatch and multi-part `iqb-standard@1.0` state; current Aspect gates metadata 2.0/spec 6.0 plus three JSON-string `iqb-standard@1.0` data parts. STARS 0.7.2 additionally gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3` and JSON-string `responses` carrying `iqb-standard@2.0`\nREADME.md:978:- source-package intake now rejects blank file names, blank media types, and unsupported source-document value types before an import job is created. Matching the Original filesystem validator, the final filename segment is limited to 120 UTF-8 bytes across upload, failed-import retry, immutable replacement, and the final `.zip` name produced by reviewed assembly; path prefixes do not consume that basename budget, and multibyte names are measured by stored bytes rather than JavaScript code units\nREADME.md:979:- loose source-package intake resolves unique original `Booklet` or `SysCheck` → `Unit` → Verona player, `DefinitionRef`, `VariablesRef`, coding-scheme, and separately uploaded `.itcr.zip` player-resource references across already uploaded workspace files. Starting the root import captures that transitive closure in a new immutable dependency-snapshot ZIP, records exact member lineage, selects the snapshot in Angular, and runs the normal importer; the original resource-package gate proves the resulting participant download in memory, file, and SQLite stores. Ambiguous references produce structured diagnostics with one Angular action per exact candidate. The chosen source-package ID is validated server-side, retained across later ambiguity decisions, and captured with the remaining unique dependency closure in the same audited immutable snapshot; incomplete matches still fail explicitly. Snapshot package and assembly evidence are committed together only if the complete source-package/activity revision still matches; otherwise the import or manual assembly returns a retryable conflict without leaving a partial aggregate. The sequential loose-file queue exposes its processed count, exact current file, accessible determinate progress, and workspace-refresh phase while disabling duplicate submission; successful files enter reviewed assembly immediately and the final best-effort report remains itemized. Manual assembly remains as the controlled fallback for deliberate 2–100-file composition, rejecting missing documents, unsafe relative paths, duplicate selection ids, case-insensitive duplicate archive paths, and per-file/aggregate size overflow while preserving an existing manifest or generating compatible IMS aliases from paths, original XML metadata, and Verona JSON-LD module identity/version metadata\nREADME.md:1035:- [packages/file-store/src/index.ts](/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/packages/file-store/src/index.ts) provides a durable JSON-file adapter for local development; its atomic manifest plus per-package/per-release sidecars keep production-sized original resources out of frequent runtime rewrites while retaining automatic legacy-file migration\nREADME.md:1051:CI runs it independently from the production-build Player smoke.\nREADME.md:1071:If `FIRST_SLICE_POSTGRES_URL` is not set, the optional Postgres test runner skips cleanly outside CI and fails in CI so a misconfigured Postgres matrix cannot pass silently. When it does run, it validates the Postgres URL scheme and parseability, then logs only a credential-redacted target. CI builds once, then uses the `:built` migration, doctor, integration, and startup scripts against the same compiled artifacts.\nREADME.md:1130:The `smoke:ui:content` variant is a fast browser slice that stops after admin/workspace bootstrap, original loose multi-file upload, automatic transitive workspace-dependency capture, explicit fallback assembly, source-package import, release activation, and the content prompt read model; it also verifies direct unit `Definition` prompt extraction. The `smoke:ui:system-check` variant executes both original system-check definitions, gates the anonymous report-save dialog plus success redirect, migrates several original-format JSON reports through Angular, verifies resumable duplicate detection across a multi-check batch, and downloads legacy-compatible CSV plus JSON. The `smoke:ui:system-check-access` variant continues through operational-login migration and proves that creating the first dedicated system-check account atomically replaces the public anonymous Start action with protected account entry, including password rotation, single-check auto-selection, required-field validation, a real report save with the forced login title, success redirect, and route isolation. The `smoke:ui:json-roster` variant continues through CSV/XML/original Testcenter `Login`/JSON roster import, saved roster export, and generated participant entry links. The `smoke:ui:participant-entry` variant continues through participant-route action gating, automatic single-Booklet sign-in, start/resume, session re-entry, direct `Definition` prompt display, completion, and local leave/reset. The `smoke:ui:participant-code` variant stops after verifying the original password-first `<Booklet codes>` challenge, invalid-code guidance, code-scoped session creation, and non-persistence of the code in browser storage. The `smoke:ui:activation-roster-warnings` variant continues to the staged-release roster compatibility warning drill-down before stopping. The `smoke:ui:review-readiness` variant continues through participant start, detailed response filtering, review creation/filtering, and the runtime review-readiness checklist. The `smoke:ui:monitor-review` variant continues through the study-monitor review queue and verifies the focused response/review handoff into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:monitor-detail-review` variant verifies booklet-detail and group-detail response/review handoffs into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:participant-detail-review` variant verifies the participant-matrix drill-down and participant-detail response/review handoff into Runtime. The `smoke:ui:monitor-bulk` variant verifies exact-id selection, confirmation, bulk pause/resume responses, and live run-state reconciliation. The `smoke:ui:delete-group-results` variant verifies result-group selection, the three selected-group CSV downloads, workspace-key-confirmed aggregate deletion, and its post-delete read-model/activity effects. The `smoke:ui:admin-session-bulk` variant verifies exact active-session selection, signed-in-session exclusion, labelled in-app confirmation, server-side delegation/audit enforcement, revocation of two live delegated bearer sessions, and automatic token/session cleanup plus reload in a second browser whose exact session was revoked. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-reset-confirmation` variant verifies the shared confirmation's safe initial focus and Escape cancellation before explicitly approving the reset, then proves old-password invalidation and the mandatory next-login change. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-change` variant covers the global account identity/role/scope panel and operator-shell sign-out plus the mandatory post-reset change and voluntary self-service path, including current-password rejection, double entry, complete session revocation, old-password invalidation, and renewed sign-in. The `smoke:ui:admin-password-bulk` variant generates a distinct 24-character password for each selected account, applies every reset through the existing delegation boundary, verifies old/new sign-in behavior, and validates the one-time CSV handoff plus in-memory cleanup. The `smoke:ui:admin-role-bulk` variant reuses the bounded exact account selection to assign one scoped role to two accounts through independent delegation checks and audit events, retaining only failures for retry. The `smoke:ui:admin-status-bulk` variant disables two delegated accounts through Angular, proves their live bearer tokens are rejected, and confirms that both session IDs are formally visible as revoked. The `smoke:ui:admin-delete` variant drives the shared confirmation across the preceding account mutations, permanently deletes two delegated accounts through Angular, verifies their directory and session removal, and requires retained deletion audits with exact role/session counts. The full SQLite variants build the Angular frontend, boot the built API process on SQLite, and drive a real browser through:\nREADME.md:1135:- original system-check execution, saved-report statistics/deletion, resumable multi-file legacy JSON migration, and original-compatible CSV/JSON report exports\nREADME.md:1156:The named `smoke:ui:verona-player-families` slice stops after executing the official Simple Player generations, the independent historical ABI 3.3.0 and current ABI 5.0.0 scripted-survey packages, current Aspect 2.12.6 assessment, historical DAN 3.0.0 and current DAN 3.1.0 visual-assessment packages, historical STARS 0.6.19 and current official STARS 0.7.2 choice-interaction, historical Speedtest 1.2.0 timed-choice and current Speedtest 3.3.0 multi-question choice, and Lottie 1.2.2 shared-parameter Players, the complete current Original STARS 0.6.40 system-test graph, the historical metadata-free `IQBVisualUnitPlayerV2.99.2` Testbed graph, and the official `verona-modules-ib` 0.2 ItemBuilder migration feasibility snapshot with DIPF runtime 9.9.0. It gates type-faithful API-2 through API-6 response restoration, including ABI 5.0.0's and DAN 3.1.0's metadata-spec-5/runtime-API-4 splits, Aspect's three JSON-string `iqb-standard@1.0` state parts, DAN's retained `IQBVisualUnitPlayerV2.1.0` state, and ABI's JSON-string `allData` response array, nested-resource delivery, automatic Player navigation, and test-wide shared-parameter restoration after reload while leaving the separate PWA offline-shell check to its dedicated smoke slice. The IB snapshot is intentionally characterized separately: its unmodified nested runtime HTML/CSS/JS/config loads and reloads through participant-isolated embeddable resources, but the legacy runtime rejects the sandboxed Player's opaque `null`-origin controller messages. Because upstream labels the repository a feasibility study rather than a release, interactive response/state parity is not claimed.\nREADME.md:1158:The named `smoke:ui:participant-confirmation` slice gates the Participant Player's labelled in-app leave confirmation against a Trial default prompt and an imported Simulation override. It verifies the safe cancel path, explicit destructive continuation, and completion after the Player's latest response has settled. It also returns a saving-mode participant from a simultaneously confirm-timed and leave-locked Unit, proving one merged dialog, one request carrying both confirmations, atomic timer cancellation plus Unit locking, and no follow-up dialog.\nREADME.md:1160:The STARS corpus retains the byte-exact metadata-2.0/API-6 Player from a fixed official Testbed commit and a radio-button definition from the matching 0.6.19 source tag as historical independent-family coverage. It also pins the current official 0.7.2 release and its byte-exact BUTTONS option-text definition from the same source tag; production SQLite/Chromium gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3`, persists its `iqb-standard@2.0` choice in JSON-string `responses`, and restores the selection after reload. Separately, the current Original Testcenter package pins the complete 0.6.40 Player/Unit/Voud/Vomd/28-alias Booklet/Testtakers graph. Its production SQLite/Chromium gate imports the unmodified assets, signs in through the original hot-return account, persists `iqb-standard@2.0` responses on aliases `1` and `2`, follows the Player's continue navigation, and restores the second selected option after reload. The dedicated `smoke:ui:stars-recovery` slice additionally proves that the bounded 200-entry browser outbox retains 56 alias-scoped responses from two valid participant runs across one actual hard reload with the active save route unavailable. It restores the visible response semantically after Player JSON reserialization, drains only that run with its visible Unit first, retains the other run exactly until its own session opens and drains visible-Unit-first, then mirrors a separate 28-Unit queue into IndexedDB on page close, replays it idempotently, and leaves both queues empty. A separate mid-drain reload settles seven of 28 responses, retains exactly the remaining 21 across the Player restart, tolerates the idempotent visible-Unit reserialization, and finishes with all server responses committed and the browser queue empty. A complete Chromium browser-process crash after the origin store has settled, followed by relaunch from the same persistent profile, proves that another complete 28-Unit queue drains without any `pagehide` handoff. At the storage boundary, a full 200-entry outbox rejects a 201st independent Unit instead of silently evicting an older response; the Participant sees the failed save, every secured entry remains byte-for-byte present, and an explicit retry persists the current answer after capacity is released.\nREADME.md:1218:## CI / Deployability\nREADME.md:1232:- [package.json](/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/package.json) exposes local CI-shaped gates: `ci:static` for typecheck/unit/build/preflight, `ci:storage` for memory/file/SQLite integration plus file/SQLite startup/shutdown, `ci:browser:quick` (including the offline App-Shell gate), `ci:browser:review`, `ci:browser:monitor`, and `ci:browser:ops` for grouped built Angular browser smokes, `ci:deployability` for file/SQLite metadata-required built-runtime preflight and startup smoke, and `ci:postgres` for the Postgres-backed migration/doctor/preflight/startup/integration/UI sequence\nREADME.md:1233:- [Dockerfile](/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/Dockerfile) provides a multi-stage production image build, runtime artifact preflight during image creation, non-root runtime user, and image-level `/readyz` healthcheck that follows the container `PORT`\nREADME.md:1245:- participant launch is still simplified, but now supports one-step starter launch, explicit tenant/workspace scoping with ambiguous workspace-key rejection, group keys, optional roster-pas