{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T07:33:42.779Z","ordinal":84420,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac5f5c59c288191bb6cc3ebbadc6278","status":"completed","call_id":"call_qOOE6lgw6Gu6zfNJ3e2OPlWl","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n # Testcenter parity checklist\\n \\n+### Atomic participant-assignment reservation foundation (2026-10-07)\\n+\\n+The repository contract now reserves or reuses a Run for the exact participant\\n+session, release and Booklet assignment atomically. It retains existing answer\\n+bytes, status, locks and timers, including completed and monitor-paused Runs;\\n+lifecycle authorization remains the application controller's responsibility.\\n+Memory makes the decision without yielding, File uses its existing single-writer\\n+mutation queue, SQLite uses an immediate transaction, and PostgreSQL locks the\\n+parent session through the same transaction client. Insert-only writes prevent\\n+a conflicting Run ID from overwriting another session or assignment.\\n+\\n+Thirty actual Memory/File/SQLite reservation checks pass, including simultaneous\\n+candidates, separate preset variants, durable reopen, invalid-scope rollback,\\n+cross-session ID collisions and four independent SQLite workers. All 315 unit/\\n+frontend checks, typecheck and the full 163-test API integration suite in each\\n+of Memory, File and SQLite pass. Native PostgreSQL reservation checks are wired\\n+into its CI runner; they have not been run locally. File continues to have a\\n+single-writer contract, not a new cross-process locking guarantee.\\n+\\n+This is a prerequisite, not a closed multi-Booklet feature: `launch` and\\n+`resumeSession` still reject a different unfinished assignment. Their integration,\\n+completion without closing another unfinished Run, guarded Starter switching,\\n+stable selected-Run URLs and real browser acceptance remain required.\\n+\\n+The published `03e660ae` full protected SQLite production browser flow also\\n+finished successfully. Its push CI separately caught an outbox-removal timeout\\n+at `smoke-ui.mjs:11508` in `participant-multi-unit-background-sync`, despite the\\n+server already receiving the answers. The root cause is not established, and\\n+the assertion has not been weakened. Neither this local reservation foundation\\n+nor a passing full browser job makes that publication globally CI-green.\\n+\\n ### Workspace and Content operator re-entry links (2026-10-07)\\n@@\\n-The complete protected SQLite flow is being repeated against an immutable copy\\n-of this production build. Fresh remote CI, PostgreSQL browser acceptance, the\\n-Memory/headful ItemBuilder failure, the multi-Booklet P0 and complete Original-UI\\n-acceptance remain separate open gates; these narrow green checks do not prove\\n-100% parity or merge readiness.\\n+The complete protected SQLite flow finished successfully against an immutable\\n+copy of this production build, with the offline App-Shell axis explicitly\\n+excluded. Fresh complete remote CI, the Memory/headful ItemBuilder failure, the\\n+multi-Booklet P0 and complete Original-UI acceptance remain separate open gates;\\n+these checks do not prove 100% parity or merge readiness.\\n@@\\n-use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself and atomic per-assignment\\n-run creation/reuse remain open; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\\n+use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself remains open. The atomic\\n+per-assignment repository reservation above is implemented and tested locally in\\n+Memory/File/SQLite, but still needs controller integration and native PostgreSQL\\n+CI evidence; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --check\\ngit check-ignore .data/assignment-run-reservation-20261007\\ngit add rewrite-app/package.json rewrite-app/packages/application/src/index.ts rewrite-app/packages/application/src/participant-assignment-runs.ts rewrite-app/packages/file-store/src/index.ts rewrite-app/packages/memory-store/src/index.ts rewrite-app/packages/postgres-store/src/index.ts rewrite-app/packages/sqlite-store/src/index.ts rewrite-app/scripts/participant-assignment-runs.test.mjs rewrite-app/scripts/run-postgres-integration.mjs rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\ngit diff --cached --stat\\ngit commit -m \\\"Reserve participant assignment runs atomically across stores\\\"\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11546-b11c-7b22-9cbf-973db5339c94","create_time":1791358403.53247}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T07:33:42.799Z","ordinal":84421,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a11546-b11c-7b22-9cbf-973db5339c94","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-1d594f1f-8549-4c48-8f19-52e2c87d0663","changes":{"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,2 +2,33 @@\n \n+### Atomic participant-assignment reservation foundation (2026-10-07)\n+\n+The repository contract now reserves or reuses a Run for the exact participant\n+session, release and Booklet assignment atomically. It retains existing answer\n+bytes, status, locks and timers, including completed and monitor-paused Runs;\n+lifecycle authorization remains the application controller's responsibility.\n+Memory makes the decision without yielding, File uses its existing single-writer\n+mutation queue, SQLite uses an immediate transaction, and PostgreSQL locks the\n+parent session through the same transaction client. Insert-only writes prevent\n+a conflicting Run ID from overwriting another session or assignment.\n+\n+Thirty actual Memory/File/SQLite reservation checks pass, including simultaneous\n+candidates, separate preset variants, durable reopen, invalid-scope rollback,\n+cross-session ID collisions and four independent SQLite workers. All 315 unit/\n+frontend checks, typecheck and the full 163-test API integration suite in each\n+of Memory, File and SQLite pass. Native PostgreSQL reservation checks are wired\n+into its CI runner; they have not been run locally. File continues to have a\n+single-writer contract, not a new cross-process locking guarantee.\n+\n+This is a prerequisite, not a closed multi-Booklet feature: `launch` and\n+`resumeSession` still reject a different unfinished assignment. Their integration,\n+completion without closing another unfinished Run, guarded Starter switching,\n+stable selected-Run URLs and real browser acceptance remain required.\n+\n+The published `03e660ae` full protected SQLite production browser flow also\n+finished successfully. Its push CI separately caught an outbox-removal timeout\n+at `smoke-ui.mjs:11508` in `participant-multi-unit-background-sync`, despite the\n+server already receiving the answers. The root cause is not established, and\n+the assertion has not been weakened. Neither this local reservation foundation\n+nor a passing full browser job makes that publication globally CI-green.\n+\n ### Workspace and Content operator re-entry links (2026-10-07)\n@@ -39,7 +70,7 @@\n \n-The complete protected SQLite flow is being repeated against an immutable copy\n-of this production build. Fresh remote CI, PostgreSQL browser acceptance, the\n-Memory/headful ItemBuilder failure, the multi-Booklet P0 and complete Original-UI\n-acceptance remain separate open gates; these narrow green checks do not prove\n-100% parity or merge readiness.\n+The complete protected SQLite flow finished successfully against an immutable\n+copy of this production build, with the offline App-Shell axis explicitly\n+excluded. Fresh complete remote CI, the Memory/headful ItemBuilder failure, the\n+multi-Booklet P0 and complete Original-UI acceptance remain separate open gates;\n+these checks do not prove 100% parity or merge readiness.\n \n@@ -218,4 +249,6 @@\n tested independently of response chronology. Legacy session-only readers still\n-use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself and atomic per-assignment\n-run creation/reuse remain open; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\n+use an `updatedAt` fallback. The launch conflict itself remains open. The atomic\n+per-assignment repository reservation above is implemented and tested locally in\n+Memory/File/SQLite, but still needs controller integration and native PostgreSQL\n+CI evidence; removing the conflict alone is not sufficient.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791358422796,"completed_at_ms":1791358422799}}
